tests:
  unit: { count: 49, covers: "Proof reads provenance: isDecryptedHttps is false for imported and sent https rows, true for a captured one beside them; its since bound excludes a captured row that started before it and admits one at or after it, and with no since an undatable row still proves. latestFlowTimes ignores imported and sent rows of either scheme. The state machine starts with no since, not-detected and re-invoke record their at as since, and goto, captured and exit keep it. useFlows counts the listings the core answered with rows, so an empty answer is told from none yet, and neither a failure nor a refusal counts. The existing flow, machine and useFlows tests still run beside them." }
  integration: { count: 92, covers: "The launch gate at render. R1 (P1 inverted): with /flows pending, the synchronous render and one 200 ms later show the checking dot and no setup question, task or statement. R2 (P2 inverted): a launch read that fails shows 'trawler is not answering' and 'no answer from <addr>' in the main area with no setup question and the dot still checking; retry reads again and an old captured row reveals the list with no banner; the stream coming back reads again without retry and an empty core then opens setup; a stream that drops while the read hangs is the same statement; the setup screen shows the statement in its band once the core goes silent, above its steps (replaces the E-UI test that pinned no band on setup). The banner: a captured row that started before setup opened reveals the list and announces nothing, one after it is announced. R3 (P6 inverted): a launch whose only https row was imported, or sent, shows setup with task 3 waiting for the first request; a sent row arriving on setup neither proves it nor reads as capturing. Review round 1's regression tests: a launch read nobody answered is not asked again before anything answers (2 reads, not 3), and the listing that ends a silent launch decides it with no read of its own. Review round 2's regression tests: a launch read that fails after a listing already answered is decided by that listing, and a recovered launch's session starts when the launch asked, so a request that started after it is announced. Review round 3's regression test: a launch read that hangs is decided by a listing that answered after it was sent. The launch read's patience: nothing is said a millisecond before LAUNCH_PATIENCE_MS, the statement is said at it, and nothing is decided. Every negative case is red against the pre-W2 App, and each round's regression tests against the tip that round reviewed." }
  e2e: { waived: "The epic plan gives the e2e journeys to W6, and pins the launch flash (R1) at App level because WebDriver cannot see a paint shorter than its poll interval. The walkthrough was re-run through the real Tauri window as evidence: green at 0880b6a, 24 reels and 144 chapters, the slow-core, core-down, imported-only and sent-only frames each showing what its caption says." }
